# Technology Stack & Dependencies

This document outlines dependency best practices when editing `package.json` files. For the full technology inventory, see [TECH_STACK.md](../../TECH_STACK.md).

## Stack Overview

### Architecture Pattern
- **Backend**: NestJS (Node.js framework) - RESTful API
- **Frontend**: React SPA with Vite
- **Database**: PostgreSQL (primary) + MongoDB (optional) + Elasticsearch (search)
- **Queue**: Bull (Redis-based) + RabbitMQ (message broker)
- **Infrastructure**: Docker, Kubernetes, Terraform
- **Cloud**: AWS (S3, Lambda)

## Backend Stack

### Core Framework

| Package | Version | Purpose | Best Practices |
|---------|---------|---------|----------------|
| `@nestjs/core` | `^10.2.10` | NestJS core framework | ✅ Latest stable v10. Use dependency injection pattern. Follow module-first architecture. |
| `@nestjs/common` | `^10.2.10` | Common NestJS utilities | ✅ Keep in sync with core version. Use decorators for validation and transformation. |
| `@nestjs/platform-express` | `^10.2.10` | Express adapter | ✅ Default HTTP adapter. Use for REST APIs. Consider Fastify for high-performance needs. |
| `typescript` | `^5.2.2` | TypeScript compiler | ✅ TypeScript 5.x with strict mode recommended. Use `strict: true` in frontend, consider enabling in backend. |

**Best Practices:**
- NestJS v10 is the latest stable major version with excellent TypeScript support
- Use decorators (`@Injectable()`, `@Controller()`, `@Module()`) consistently
- Leverage dependency injection for testability
- Follow the module-per-feature pattern

### Database & ORM

| Package | Version | Purpose | Best Practices |
|---------|---------|---------|----------------|
| `typeorm` | `^0.3.17` | TypeORM ORM | ⚠️ **Version Note**: v0.3.x is the latest. Use Entity classes with decorators. Consider migrations for schema changes. |
| `pg` | `^8.11.3` | PostgreSQL driver | ✅ Latest stable. Use connection pooling. Configure SSL for production. |
| `mongoose` | `^8.0.3` | MongoDB ODM | ✅ Latest v8.x. Use schemas with TypeScript interfaces. Enable strict mode. |
| `@nestjs/typeorm` | `^10.0.1` | NestJS TypeORM integration | ✅ Keep in sync with NestJS version. Use repository pattern. |
| `@nestjs/mongoose` | `^10.0.2` | NestJS Mongoose integration | ✅ Use for MongoDB operations. Consider using alongside TypeORM if needed. |

**Best Practices:**
- **TypeORM v0.3.x**: Breaking changes from v0.2.x. Use DataSource instead of Connection.
- Use migrations for all schema changes
- Enable query logging in development, disable in production
- Use transactions for multi-step operations
- Consider using repository pattern for complex queries

